## Step 14: the raise
I judged each payment the body lists. (1) and (3) are sound refusals. (2) is right: whichever half carries the law carries all 36 re-plans. (4) and (5) are the ruling's own choices. archscore reads only custom_components, and the entry is JSON, so dS 0 is honest. The counts are earned by the change: CI's stress log ties every uncovered scenario to "re-planned by this branch", none new or dropped. I found no missed payment that would improve the code.

I did find one soundness defect in the diff's own gate rule, to fix in the re-cut. `coverage_floors` accepts a `calls_floor` anywhere below share(40)=15, not below share(floor). But `budget_raise_gate` treats withdrawing an OVERRIDE leaf as always routine, and its new self-test claims "withdrawn is routine (the share rule is stricter)". Demonstrated (ev/calls_floor_withdraw.txt): `{floor 18, calls_floor 10}` gives (18, 10); withdrawing calls_floor gives (18, 7); `file_raises` returns []. So a later branch can lower the production-call floor from 10 to 7 with no approval. Fix: bound `calls_floor` by `share(floor)` in `coverage_floors`, or have the gate price the withdrawal against share(floor).

## Nit
thermal_model.py:2050 (compute_cop's docstring) still says compute_cop_dhw "starts from _cop_law with no curve flow". It now passes the tank temperature as the flow. "No curve flow" is still literally true, but the line should say the tank's own water temperature is the flow.
